    <statement><p>A car rental company charges a one-time application fee of 30 dollars, 
50 dollars per day, and 11 cents per mile for its cars.</p>
<p>(a) Write a formula for the cost, <m>C</m>, of renting a car as a function of the
number of days, <m>d</m>, and the number of miles driven, <m>m</m>.</p>
<p><m>C =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) If <m>C = f(d, m)</m>, then <m>f(4, 870) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>30+50d+\frac{11m}{100}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>325.7</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
